Description: Keel overlay: Syncthing, the file replication of a pair
 The Syncthing overlay of Keel Linux (handbook decision 0050): the unit
 that runs the binary package as the syncthing user, and the overlay
 manifest keel reads, installed as
 /usr/share/keel/overlays/syncthing.yaml (decision 0041).
 .
 The service is installed disabled and stopped, the state of a simple
 installation: keel spec apply enables it with the overlay. keel renders
 the configuration from the application manifests and the role, and adds
 the replicated paths to the unit with a drop-in.
 .
 The unit holds CAP_CHOWN, CAP_FOWNER and CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE as ambient
 capabilities, so a received file keeps the owner of the application's
 directory (copyOwnershipFromParent) without root, and ProtectSystem=
 strict with write access to the home only.
